      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if the interval crosses zero, does that mean my model is basically unreliable? it feels like there's this weird contradiction where one number says \"yes\" and the other says \"maybe not.\" is there a specific way to describe this kind of uncertainty in my methodology chapter so it doesn't look like my data is just messy or full of errors?",
